<title>UK: Bradford wool market remains mostly unchanged.</title>
<headline>Bradford wool market remains mostly unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>BRADFORD 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Selling levels at the Bradford wool sale remained mostly unmoved due to holiday factors, traders said.</p>
<p>The few increases in topmakers quotations, probably reflected the minor rise posted in the main wool market indicators, they added.</p>
<p>Types 70's super and 66's super rose five pence per kilo and two pence respectively, while the rest were unchanged.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 8074</p>
